Nature of the modifications
---------------------------
This fork extends upstream's resource coverage of the RouterOS configuration
tree and relaxes several schema constraints that prevented importing the
configuration of a live device. Specifically:

  * Additional resources covering RouterOS menus not represented upstream,
    raising the registered resource count from 254 to 415. COVERAGE.md lists
    them.

  * Schema fields present in RouterOS 7.23 but absent from upstream's schema,
    which caused values to be silently dropped on read. Among them:
    bridge ra-guard / dhcpv6-snooping / MLAG attributes, bridge-port
    trusted-ra / trusted-dhcpv6 / actual-path-cost, veth dhcp-address and
    container-mac-address, DHCP-server add-dns-entries, and adlist comment.

  * Validation relaxations where upstream's constraints were stricter than
    RouterOS itself: optional route gateway, optional netwatch name, BGP TTL
    lower bound of 0 rather than 1, and bridge-port BPDU-guard accepting the
    boolean form the REST API actually returns.

